<odoo>
    <data noupdate="0">

        <!--
            =============    This was created by Srivatsan Ji, doesn't satisfy the required condition, 
            hence commented out the code and added a new code to achieve the required functionality. ============
            
            Sales visibility rules — restricted-by-email salespeople (PRIVATE).
            Users in RESTRICTED_LOGINS see only their own sale orders / lines.
            Their orders / lines are HIDDEN from EVERY OTHER user, including
            admins (base.group_system).

            Caveat: the original Odoo superuser (login='admin', uid=1) bypasses
            ALL ir.rule by design. To block superuser too, a Python override on
            sale.order._search / read would be required (separate change).

            To add or remove a user from the restricted list, edit the two
            email lists below (in BOTH rules) and re-upgrade `contact_stage_bar`.

            Odoo ships these rules with noupdate="1", so we wrap the override
            with the same ir.model.data write trick used elsewhere in this module.

            Go to Settings → Technical → Security → Record Rules
            You'll see 3 rules — "All Orders", "All Orders Lines", "All Orders Analysis"
            Open each one and reset the Domain back to Odoo's default (usually [(1, '=', 1)] for the "see all" rules, meaning no restriction).

            If wanted to make it restriced again for Aarav & Ankit, the domain to apply would be:
             ['|', ('salesman_id', '=', user.id), '&', ('salesman_id.login', 'not in', ['ankit.mehta@augmont.com', 'aarav.bafna@augmont.com']), (user.login not in ['ankit.mehta@augmont.com','aarav.bafna@augmont.com'], '=', True)]
        -->

